[{:adr/authoritative_for ["kotoba.ontology: object-type registry seeded with :tender, generalizing goyoukiki.model/opportunity's common denominator" "kotoba.ontology.connector: connector registry (jp.kkj, jp.geps) + pure `tag` stamping :ontology/type :ontology/source :ontology/fetched-at :ontology/confidence provenance onto an already-normalized fact" "kotoba-lang capability-library skeleton confirmed (LICENSE/README/deps.edn/ci.yml/src+test, no governance docs, no docs/adr — that belongs to cloud-itonami-* blueprints not capability libs)" "in-source `def` registry chosen over resources/*.edn + slurp (JVM-only pattern in kotoba.industry/kotoba.technology is grandfathered, not to be copied into new code per runtime-priority rule)" "kotoba-lang/technology registry.edn gets one new entry (:id :ontology) so :required-technologies can name it — the only existing-repo change, landed via isolated worktree + server-side merge, not in-place shared-checkout edit" "explicitly out of scope: wiring any cloud-itonami-* blueprint's required-technologies to :ontology, any kotoba-lang/industry per-ISIC entry, further object types beyond :tender, .ui/.export namespaces"], :adr/supersedes [], :adr/superseded_by [], :adr/topic "kotoba-lang-ontology-connector-registry", :adr/related ["adr-2607070300-kotoba-lang-goyoukiki-jp-real-ingestion-connectors" "adr-2607070200-kotoba-lang-goyoukiki-procurement-signal-actor"], :adr/status "proposed", :adr/id "adr-2607110500-kotoba-lang-ontology-connector-registry", :adr/doc_type "adr", :adr/last_verified "2026-07-10", :adr/body "# ADR-2607110500: kotoba-lang/ontology — object-type + connector provenance registry\n\n**Status**: proposed\n**Date**: 2026-07-10\n**Deciders**: Jun Kawasaki\n\n## Context\n\nOwner asked whether cloud-itonami has anything like Palantir. Found a real Foundry/AIP-shaped core already in place (kotoba datom log, activity/decision/effect/audit, advisor⊣governor pattern, org/repo tenant namespace) but two real gaps: no shared object-type vocabulary and no generalized external-data connector foundation beyond kotoba-lang/goyoukiki's per-vertical jp.kkj/jp.geps (ADR-2607070300). Owner chose to build the connector/ontology foundation and realize it as a real new child repo via the standard project-creation flow. Researched conventions first: kotoba-lang capability libraries (robotics/phone/industry/technology) share a light skeleton with no governance boilerplate and no docs/adr (that belongs to cloud-itonami-* blueprints); kotoba-lang/technology's registry.edn is the fleet-wide SSoT mapping a required-technologies keyword to its implementing repo(s).\n\n## Decision\n\nAdd kotoba-lang/ontology as a capability library (not a cloud-itonami-* blueprint). kotoba.ontology: object-type registry seeded with one real type, :tender, generalizing goyoukiki.model/opportunity. kotoba.ontology.connector: registry of jp.kkj/jp.geps (both real, both already tested) plus a pure `tag` fn stamping :ontology/* provenance onto an already-normalized fact — no I/O in either namespace, fetch/parse stays in goyoukiki's own JVM adapters. Skeleton mirrors robotics/phone/technology (Apache-2.0, README with an explicit Non-goals section, deps.edn test+lint aliases, ci.yml, no governance docs/docs-adr). Registry data is an in-source def, not resources/*.edn+slurp, since that JVM-only pattern in kotoba.industry/kotoba.technology is grandfathered legacy, not a template for new code under the runtime-priority rule. Added one entry to kotoba-lang/technology's registry.edn (:id :ontology) so the keyword becomes nameable in blueprint.edn's required-technologies — landed via an isolated worktree + server-side merge, since the shared orgs/kotoba-lang/technology checkout's branch changed under this session mid-task (confirmed multi-agent shared-checkout hazard).\n\n## Consequences\n\nCloses the two identified Palantir-comparison gaps, honestly scoped from what already exists and is tested rather than invented ahead of need. goyoukiki's two connectors get a shared index and common provenance tag with zero changes to goyoukiki itself. 5 tests/15 assertions green, clj-kondo clean, verified before commit. Only one object type and two connectors seeded — broader coverage, blueprint adoption of :required-technologies [:ontology], and any .ui/.export namespace are explicit follow-up, not delivered here. Still not Foundry-scale: no pipeline/ETL builder, no connector marketplace, no Gotham-style product.\n\n## References\n\nADR-2607070300, ADR-2607070200, gftdcojp/cloud-itonami docs/adr/0002-org-repo-tenant-isolation.md, kotoba-lang/technology resources/kotoba/technology/registry.edn.", :adr/deciders ["Jun Kawasaki"], :adr/date "2026-07-10", :db/id -1, :adr/authoritative true, :adr/title "ADR-2607110500: kotoba-lang/ontology — object-type + connector provenance registry"}]
